1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--the-noticing-game","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/the-noticing-game","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/the-noticing-game","sourceHash":"0f6001ee5357e12189bcc718be7c5c80c0564c70b833aa88d70060e0fda95458","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:10.830Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"The Noticing Game","zh":"留意游戏"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Noticing Game is a beginner immersion technique for when you can't understand much of what's happening in the target language. Instead of trying to understand, your goal is simply to <em>notice</em> things: words you recognize, sounds that repeat, patterns that stand out.","zh":"留意游戏是一种适合初学者的沉浸技巧，适用于你还无法理解目标语言中大部分内容的阶段。你的目标不是努力理解，而只是<em>留意</em>各种信息：你认识的词、反复出现的声音，以及格外显眼的模式。"}},{"id":"how-to-play","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Play","zh":"玩法"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Put on some content in the target language (a TV show, video, podcast — anything)","zh":"播放一些目标语言内容（电视剧、视频、播客——任何内容都可以）"},{"en":"Instead of trying to understand the meaning, focus on spotting things you recognize","zh":"不要试图理解含义，而是专注于发现自己认识的内容"},{"en":"Listen for words you've learned in vocab study, sounds you studied, or patterns you've seen before","zh":"留意你在词汇学习中学过的词、练习过的语音，或以前见过的语言模式"},{"en":"When you notice something, mentally acknowledge it (\"I heard that word!\" or \"that sounds familiar\")","zh":"当你注意到某个内容时，在心里确认一下（“我听到那个词了！”或“这个听起来很熟悉”）"},{"en":"If your focus wanders, remind yourself to look for things and continue","zh":"如果注意力飘走了，提醒自己继续寻找能注意到的内容"}]},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"That's it. No pausing, no looking things up, no stress about understanding.","zh":"就是这样。不暂停，不查资料，也不必为是否理解而感到压力。"}},{"id":"why-it-works","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Works","zh":"为什么有效"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"As a beginner, trying to <em>understand</em> content in a language you barely know is frustrating and demotivating. The Noticing Game reframes the task: instead of feeling like you're failing to understand, you're succeeding at finding things. This keeps you engaged with the language and gives your brain meaningful practice processing it.","zh":"作为初学者，试图<em>理解</em>一门你几乎不了解的语言中的内容，既令人沮丧，又会打击学习动力。“留意游戏”重新定义了这项任务：你不再觉得自己没能理解内容，而是因成功发现了一些东西而获得成就感。这能让你持续投入这门语言，也让大脑得到有意义的语言处理练习。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It also strengthens the connection between what you study (priming) and what you encounter in real content (immersion). When you notice a word you studied, your brain reinforces that knowledge.","zh":"它还能加强你所学习的内容（预备学习）与你在真实内容中遇到的内容（沉浸）之间的联系。当你注意到一个学过的词时，大脑就会巩固相关知识。"}},{"id":"leveling-up","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Leveling Up","zh":"进阶"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Once the basic Noticing Game feels easy, try the <strong>Noticing Game with Confirmation</strong>: when you notice something, pause and try to remember what it means. Then check with a dictionary or tool. This is a step toward interactive immersion — you're starting to decode the language, not just notice it.","zh":"当基础版“留意游戏”变得轻松后，可以尝试<strong>带确认环节的留意游戏</strong>：注意到某个内容时，先暂停一下，试着回想它的意思，然后用词典或其他工具核对。这是迈向互动式沉浸的一步——你开始解读这门语言，而不只是留意它。"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"小贴士"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Keep a list of recently learned words handy to give yourself things to look for","zh":"把最近学过的词汇列表放在手边，让自己随时有内容可留意"},{"en":"Content with visual context (TV, video) is easier than pure audio","zh":"带有视觉语境的内容（电视节目、视频）比纯音频更容易"},{"en":"Don't worry about understanding the story. That's not the point yet.","zh":"不用担心是否理解故事情节。现阶段的重点并不在此。"},{"en":"Even 10-15 minutes of the Noticing Game is valuable practice","zh":"即使只进行 10～15 分钟的“留意游戏”，也是很有价值的练习"}]},{"id":"when-to-use-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Use It","zh":"何时使用"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The Noticing Game is most useful in Phases 1A-1C, when your vocabulary is still too small for meaningful comprehension. As your vocabulary grows and you start understanding more, you'll naturally transition to Interactive Reading with Audio.","zh":"“留意游戏”在阶段 1A～1C 最有用，因为此时你的词汇量还不足以形成有意义的理解。随着词汇量增加、理解的内容越来越多，你会自然过渡到带音频的互动式阅读。"}},{"id":"segment-0014","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<a href=\"/roadmap/library/interactive-reading-with-audio\">Interactive Reading with Audio</a>","zh":"<a href=\"/roadmap/library/interactive-reading-with-audio\">带音频的互动式阅读</a>"}}],"cards":[]}}]
